  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Hungarian DominÃ³ (Block). 2-4 players, 28-tile Double-Six dominoes. Deal: 2p=12 tiles, 3p=8 tiles, 4p=6 tiles each. Highest double leads. Play: Match pips at chain ends. Pass if no legal move. Block: Both chain ends same number = board block. Scoring: Winner takes opponent pip totals. Avoidance: Lowest score wins.',
    Player: "Welcome to Hungarian DominÃ³. You're playing the Block variantâ€”no boneyard, just pure hand management. Build a linear chain of matching dominoes. Try to force your opponents to pass while you empty your hand. In traditional play, lowest score winsâ€”it's an avoidance game. Watch what your opponents pass on; that tells you their weaknesses.",
    objective: 'Win the round by playing all tiles in your hand, or by having the lowest total pips when the game is blocked.',
    gameplay: '1. The player with the highest double leads (or highest tile if no doubles).\n2. Players must match the pips of an open end of the linear layout.\n3. **Blocking**: If you cannot match an end, you pass your turn.\n4. The layout is restricted to two ends; doubles are placed crosswise but do not create new lines.',
    keyRules: [
      'Follow the legal action constraints defined for Hungarian DominÃ³ (Block).',
      "Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: The winner scores the total sum of pips remaining in all opponents' hands.",
      'Winning condition: Win the round by playing all tiles in your hand, or by having the lowest total pips when the game is blocked.',
